State machine
=============

      entry:
        transport telnet -> state_login_telnet
    
      state_login_telnet
          login              -> send user              -> pw
          password           -> send password          -> at_shell
      pw
          password           -> send password          -> at_shell
      at_shell
          at prompt          -> send conf              -> at_conf
      at_conf
          at prompt          -> send show command      -> capture
      capture
          at prompt          -> capture_stop           -> done
          (capture_start on entry)

States
======

State               Waits for (expect)   Action                                     Next
------------------  -------------------  -----------------------------------------  --------
state_login_telnet  /login: $/           send user                                  pw
                    /password: $/        send_secret pass                           at_shell
pw                  /password: $/        send_secret pass                           at_shell
at_shell            /\/>$/               send "conf"                                at_conf
at_conf             /\/CONFiguration>$/  send show_cmd                              capture
capture             /\/CONFiguration>$/  capture_start on entry, then capture_stop  done

States with more than one expect try them in order; the first match wins.

Template source
===============

Full source of templates/mediant.tmpl:

    # mediant.tmpl - AudioCodes Mediant gateway (telnet, menu CLI).
    #
    # syntax_style: generic
    #
    # Derived from fetchconfig::model::Mediant. Log in, enter the config context
    # with "conf", then dump the ini with "cf get". The prompts are fixed strings
    # ("/>" shell, "/CONFiguration>" config), not hostname-based, so they are
    # matched explicitly.
    # Note: DRAFT - please verify on real hardware.
    
    transport      telnet
    banner_timeout 30
    fetch_timeout  120
    max_visits     8
    
    # dump command "cf get"; override per device with show_cmd=.
    show_cmd       'cf get'
    
    # drop the echoed "cf get" command line
    skip_first     1
    
    # ---- telnet entry: interactive login ----
    state state_login_telnet
        expect /login: $/          -> send user        -> goto pw
        expect /password: $/       -> send_secret pass   -> goto at_shell
    
    state pw
        expect /password: $/       -> send_secret pass   -> goto at_shell
    
    # shell prompt "/>": enter the config context
    state at_shell
        expect /\/>$/              -> send "conf"       -> goto at_conf
    
    # config prompt "/CONFiguration>": dump the ini
    state at_conf
        expect /\/CONFiguration>$/ -> send show_cmd      -> goto capture
    
    state capture
        capture_start
        expect /\/CONFiguration>$/ -> capture_stop       -> done

